The [[Genus|genera]] of duckweeds are: ''[[Spirodela]]'', ''[[Landoltia]]'', ''[[Lemna]]'', ''[[Wolffiella]]'', and ''[[Wolffia]]''.

Duckweed [[genome]] sizes have a ten-fold range (150~1,500&nbsp;MB), potentially representing [[Ploidy#Diploid|diploids]] to [[Polyploid|octaploids]]. The ancestral genus of ''Spirodela'' has the smallest genome size (150&nbsp;MB, similar to ''[[Arabidopsis thaliana]]''), while the most derived genus, ''Wolffia'', contains plants with the largest genome size (1,500&nbsp;MB).<ref>{{cite journal |author1=Wang, Wenqin |author2=Kerstetter, Randall A. |author3=Michael, Todd P. |title=Evolution of Genome Size in Duckweeds (''Lemnaceae'')|journal=Journal of Botany|year=2011|volume=2011|doi=10.1155/2011/570319|issn=2090-0120|issue=570319|pages=1–9|doi-access=free}}</ref> [[DNA sequencing]] has shown that ''Wolffiella'' and ''Wolffia'' are more closely related than the others. ''Spirodela'' is at the [[Basal (phylogenetics)|basal]] position of the taxon, followed by ''Lemna'', ''Wolffiella'', and ''Wolffia'', which is the most derived.<ref>{{cite journal|last=Wang|first=Wenqin|author2=Messing, Joachim |author3=Badger, Jonathan H. |year=2011 |title=High-Throughput sequencing of three ''Lemnoideae'' (duckweeds) chloroplast genomes from total DNA |journal=PLOS ONE |volume=6 |issue=9 |article-number =e24670 |doi=10.1371/journal.pone.0024670 |doi-access=free |pmc=3170387 |pmid=21931804|bibcode=2011PLoSO...624670W}}</ref>
